From 0974c4908d576ca3f2b20d8ff829ce4c5c8a0575 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anthonybartczak <49080651+anthonybartczak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:56:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Abandon an unfinished header only after one more frame

A header whose message was still missing bytes was stepped over as
soon as a whole notification lay behind it. But what lies behind an
unfinished header is inside its declared body, and a notification that
carried the bytes of another one as data, cut after them, lost its own
header that way.

Two things together now show that a header was false: it has already
waited through a whole frame, since the device sends a message in two
frames at most, and a whole notification has arrived behind it. A
false header in front of whole notifications is therefore stepped over
one frame later than before, and no later.

The 70 507 messages in the HX Edit captures pass through as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
